{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RightDualIsoUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RightDualIsoUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.coev_comp_rightDualIso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.coev_comp_rightDualIso","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RightDualIsoUnique.lean#L82-L110","doc":"**The coevaluation identity that characterises `rightDualIso`** — the mirror of\n`rightDualIso_hom_evaluation`.\n\nWhere the evaluation form says the comparison of two right duals commutes with the two evaluations,\nthis says it carries one coevaluation to the other.  Proved by transporting both sides through\n`tensorLeftHomEquiv` *for the pairing `p₁`* — the choice matters: the `p₂` equivalence leaves a\nmixed `η_{p₂}` against `ε_{p₁}` that is no snake, while the `p₁` one reduces each side to\n`(ρ_ B₁).hom ≫ (rightDualIso p₁ p₂).hom` after one use of the evaluation form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualIso_hom_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualIso_hom_trans","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RightDualIsoUnique.lean#L74-L80","doc":"**Comparisons of right duals compose.**  Immediate from uniqueness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualIso_hom_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualIso_hom_unique","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RightDualIsoUnique.lean#L64-L72","doc":"**The comparison of two right duals is unique.**  Any map commuting with the evaluations *is*\n`rightDualIso`.  Mathlib has `rightDualIso` and `rightDualIso_id` and nothing else about it, so\nthis is the missing characterisation — and it is what makes the comparison usable in proofs, since\nit turns \"construct the map\" into \"check one identity\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualIso_hom_evaluation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualIso_hom_evaluation","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RightDualIsoUnique.lean#L57-L62","doc":"**The evaluation identity that characterises `rightDualIso`.**  `rightAdjointMate` of the\nidentity, read through `rightAdjointMate_comp_evaluation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.whiskerRight_evaluation_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.whiskerRight_evaluation_injective","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RightDualIsoUnique.lean#L48-L55","doc":"**Pairing against the evaluation is injective.**  This is what makes a mate identifiable from\nthe identity it satisfies, and is the cancellation step in `swap_mate_mate`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.tensorRightHomEquiv_whiskerRight_evaluation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.tensorRightHomEquiv_whiskerRight_evaluation","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RightDualIsoUnique.lean#L37-L46","doc":"Pairing a morphism against the evaluation is, under `tensorRightHomEquiv`, the morphism itself\n(up to a unitor).  The snake identity, with the morphism carried out of the way by\n`whisker_exchange`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}